IENT_FS faults are observable to operators.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"run_git(..., retry=RetryPolicy) that folds the timeout shims\"","No mention of logging/metric on retry attempts; ABSENCE rationale — reliability overlay applies because run_git adds/consolidates a retry failure path"],"finding":"The shared run_git consolidates retry behavior (LOCK / TRANSIENT_FS ride-out) that previously lived at five sites, but the plan does not state whether retry attempts emit a log/metric. Given the two originating bugs (unheedful-custodial-bluebottle, wrongful-chemic-squeaker) were silent classification/retry drift, operator visibility into how often TRANSIENT_FS/LOCK faults are being ridden out is relevant.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f15efc71efc67a581","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — run_git(..., retry=RetryPolicy); Acceptance Criteria AC-2","norm_id":"nd67dcf45a79bf369","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A merge silently retries TRANSIENT_FS faults many times, masking a systemic FS problem operators never see"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a line to Approach: run_git emits a debug/info log (or counter) on each retry naming the GitOutcome kind and operation; no new AC required if a pinning test already asserts the log.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified"